[2025-04-14 22:05:00,872][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                        &lt;strong&gt;Microsoft Credits EncryptHub, Hacker Behind 618+ Breaches, for Disclosing Windows Flaws (3 minute read)&lt;/strong&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:00,872][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                    &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:00,872][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "&lt;/a&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:00,872][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:00,872][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:00,872][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:00,872][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                    Microsoft has credited EncryptHub for uncovering Windows security flaws, highlighting a conflicted figure in cybersecurity and cybercrime. EncryptHub, or SkorikARI, was linked to multiple malware campaigns against high-value targets. Despite its technical skill, EncryptHub&apos;s inadequate security practices ultimately led to exposure and arrest during the Russo-Ukrainian war.[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:00,873][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
