[2025-04-14 22:05:01,051][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                &lt;a href=&quot;https://tracking.tldrnewsletter.com/CL0/https:%2F%2Fostro.ws%2Fpost-timing-attacks%3Futm_source=tldrinfosec/1/01000195dce3cb04-ff7d9d86-f278-4f1c-bb1e-f8d0da35abc8-000000/QRMcAR606L1Arqay8zvPH-FMaQkvHtRB7xcCD_LozWU=398&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:01,051][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                    &lt;span&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:01,051][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                        &lt;strong&gt;Fun with Timing Attacks (10 minute read)&lt;/strong&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:01,051][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                    &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:01,051][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "&lt;/a&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:01,051][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:01,051][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:01,051][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:01,051][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                    Timing attacks can exploit non-constant-time string comparison functions like `startsWith` to determine secrets character by character. Attackers can deduce when a guess&apos;s prefix matches part of the secret by measuring execution times over many trials, allowing them to crack an 8-character password in just thousands of attempts rather than billions. This can be demonstrated with a browser-based implementation using Thompson Sampling and a statistical approach. Developers should avoid direct secret comparisons and instead use proper cryptographic hashing with rate limiting.[\n]"
[2025-04-14 22:05:01,051][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-0 << "                                &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
